Description: split Asterisk modules into Zamfono functional packages
 Replaces Debian's single asterisk-modules binary package with one binary
 package per functional group, and turns asterisk-modules into an
 Architecture: all meta-package depending on every group at
 ${binary:Version}. The asterisk package depends on asterisk-modules-core
 alone. The internal test modules are not built or shipped; TEST_FRAMEWORK
 itself stays enabled because AST_BUILDOPT_SUM, which debian/rules checks
 against SAVED_ABI_HASH, covers it.
 .
 The Breaks/Replaces entries naming Debian's former module packages
 (asterisk-mp3, asterisk-dahdi, ...) are deliberately unversioned: a
 substvar version bound against a package built from a different source
 package, e.g. asterisk-mp3 (<< ${source:Version}), raises lintian's
 version-substvar-for-external-package error, which the lintian gate
 rejects.
Author: Zamfono Packaging <packages@zamfono.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
